<title>SWEDEN: AssiDoman posts 61 pct slump '96 profit.</title>
<headline>AssiDoman posts 61 pct slump '96 profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish forestry group AssiDoman posts its earnings for the 12 months ending December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		  1,713 vs   4,346</p>
<p> Turnover				   19,316 vs  21,836</p>
<p> EPS (skr)				   11.90 vs   28.90</p>
<p> Proposed dividend (SKR)		  5.25 vs    5.00</p>
<p> Operating costs			  16,265 vs  16,387</p>
<p> Depreciation				1,144 vs   1,011</p>
<p> Associate interests		 CHARGE 64 vs	35 CREDIT</p>
<p> Operating profit after deprec	 1,843 vs   4,473</p>
<p> Net financial items		CHARGE 130 vs     127 CHARGE</p>
<p> Tax					     306 vs     927</p>
<p> Minorities					0 vs	 1 CHARGE</p>
<p> Net profit				  1,407 vs   3,418</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuters poll found the market expected AssiDoman to post a profit after financial items of 1.95 billion crowns with forecasts varying between 1.37 billion and 2.18 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
